  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the range (difference between maximum and minimum outcomes) of each lottery, favoring the one with the smaller range. The individual considered the outcomes and specifically emphasized the absence of risk of loss in Lottery B, which aligns with recognizing that Lottery A has both high and low outcomes (including a large loss), while Lottery B has no variation. Although the individual did not explicitly mention the range, the focus on avoiding any possibility of loss directly relates to the minimum outcome, and the preference for certainty aligns with preferring a smaller outcome range. The reasoning is consistent with the core idea of the decision reason—avoiding spread through aversion to downside risk—even if not framed in terms of range calculation. The emphasis on 'no risk of losing money' reflects sensitivity to the full spread of outcomes, particularly the worst-case scenario, which is a key component of the range-based reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}
